From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:36:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] about: match Mihon's update UI (no post-update dialog,
 release page for What's new)

KMK shows an "Updated to vX" dialog on the first launch after an update,
and both its "What's new" button and the About screen's "What's new" entry
open an in-app screen that fetches the newest GitHub release and shows
"Latest: <tag> - Current: <versionName>". Right after installing that very
version this reads like the app offering the same version again, and it
differs from Mihon, which has no such dialog and opens the release page of
the installed version in the browser.

- MainActivity: drop the WhatsNewDialog block and the preview_last_version_code
  bookkeeping; Migrator.awaitAndRelease() is called as in Mihon.
- AboutScreen: "What's new" opens RELEASE_URL; remove the getReleaseNotes
  helper that only served the removed flows.

"Check for updates" is unchanged: it already compares the (major, minor,
patch, harmony) tuple and toasts "No new updates available" when the
installed build is the latest release.
